# Engineering Backbone adoption

This directory contains the selected foundation and project facts. Language and
frontend/backend flags are descriptive metadata; they do not invent application
commands, workflows or required infrastructure.

- Review [project facts](project.json) and the [canonical policy](core.md).
- Integrate [agent guidance](AGENTS.fragment.md) and
  [Copilot guidance](Copilot.fragment.md) into existing stronger instructions.
- Existing `AGENTS.md`, Copilot instructions, native role profiles and project
  facts are preserved, including during updates. New files are created only when
  absent. Later baseline changes therefore require a reviewed manual refresh of
  those entrypoints/profiles; a successful Copier update alone is not full adoption.
- Commit `copier-answers.yml` and use an explicit reviewed Git commit or release
  reference for updates. Review core and fragment changes, refresh protected files
  as needed, and run project checks before merging the update PR.
- Never use automatic merge or publish the baseline from the generated project.

The template has no tasks, migrations or shell hooks. The validation command is
recorded as data; Copier never runs it. Native role definitions need a supported
local Codex/Copilot client and runtime verification. GitHub code-review settings
must be configured separately.

Install the generated validator's pinned, hashed dependencies in an isolated
Python 3.12 environment:
`python -m pip install --require-hashes -r .engineering-backbone/requirements.lock`.
Then run `python .engineering-backbone/validate.py --root .`. The companion
`requirements.txt` records direct dependencies; lock compilation is central
maintenance, not a template execution hook.

From the consumer repository, invoke updates with the namespaced answers file:
`copier update --answers-file .engineering-backbone/copier-answers.yml --vcs-ref APPROVED_COMMIT`.
Replace the reference with a reviewed commit; this command prepares a diff for review.

The installation choices `use_codex`, `use_copilot`, and `backbone_workflow_ref`
cannot change during a normal template update. The update rejects such changes
before consumer rendering. Adapter changes require their own reviewed migration
of native files, project facts and installation choices. Do not edit or remove
answers merely to bypass this guard.

For a first adoption, leave the workflow choice empty and merge the reviewed seed
bundle with the caller inactive. Add the pinned caller from
[the workflow example](workflow-example.md) in a separate activation PR. A manually
maintained caller can be activated, removed or repinned through a reviewed workflow
migration without changing the saved template-generation choice. The shared gate
executes only the trusted consumer base's validator and dependencies; absent or
partial baselines fail closed. SHA values render in lowercase and existing caller
pins remain preserved during ordinary Copier updates.
